# publicise deny-list — strings that must never reach the published copy.
#
# One fixed string per line. Matched case-insensitively against the OUTPUT of
# tests/publicise.sh, after every redaction rule has run. A hit refuses the transform
# and writes nothing, so the file this repo publishes cannot contain it.
#
# This is the EXAMPLE. The real list is machine-local and is deliberately not committed
# here: a deny-list in a public repo publishes the exact strings it exists to withhold.
#
#   cp tests/publicise-deny.example ~/.claude/publicise-deny.txt
#   $EDITOR ~/.claude/publicise-deny.txt
#
# Override the path with PUBLICISE_DENY=/some/other/file.
#
# Good entries are the names that only mean something inside your own setup: private
# project and product lines, private repo names, your username, absolute home paths,
# and the filenames of any local file a redaction rule folds out.

YOUR-PRIVATE-PROJECT
your-private-source-repo
your-username
/Users/
/home/
